module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.dotted_reference_truncated_at_v2_body_lowering

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, WholeDeclaration }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data dotted_reference_truncated_at_v2_body_lowering: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "dotted_reference_truncated_at_v2_body_lowering" as NonEmptyStr,
  receipts: [
    "**a dotted reference is lowered to a PREFIX of itself and the lowering Accepts** (INVALID STATE: v2.compiler.normalize, via v2.compiler.body_lowering_fold, lowered a postfix chain `a.b.c.d` in a BODY to Transform(dag_token_dot, a, b) -- the first dot read as a binary operator by an operand reader that accepted ANY lex token as an operator -- and lowered a qualified name `a.b.C` in a TYPE position to the bare atom `a`. In both arms every later segment was dropped and nothing refused. The tree the resolver and the reference-site collector received carried two or three bare mentions of module-path segments and no mention of the target.)",
    "HARM. Two consumers read the truncated tree as fact. v2.compiler.resolve refused every cross-module reference as an unbound `a` -- a TRUE refusal for the WRONG reason, which is how the class hid: the module was red, so nobody read the tree. v2.compiler.reference_site_collector saw zero qualified sites over the production route, so the XL-0 denominator and the XL-4 reference graph both undercounted exactly the class an import-to-containment cut is made of, and gunbc.compiler_frontend_program_status StageXL0Denominator sat NOT-DERIVABLE on a capability nobody owned. Had the reference been to a name that ALSO existed bare in scope, the first segment would have bound and the module would have been Accepted with a fabricated meaning.",
    "DISTINGUISHING FACTS, against the neighbour that looks like it. call_expression_erased_at_v2_body_lowering drops a CALL's callee and arguments; this row drops the TAIL of a REFERENCE that has no call at all, and the two are restored by different arms -- restoring calls leaves a dotted value reference truncated, and restoring dotted references leaves a dotted CALLEE with the call class. The recognition rule: the lowered node is a strict prefix of the surface spelling and the lowering reported no loss.",
    "RECEIPT (2026-09-18, smart-lynx-554). On the production route (v2.compiler.program_assembly module_roots_from_source_root_ingest projected through v2.compiler.normalized_tree) a body `v2.test.xl0_provider.xl0_provided_value` dumped as Transform(dag_token_dot, v2, test); a parameter type `v2.test.xl0_provider.T` dumped as Atom v2; resolution of the module refused resolve_reason_unbound_symbol while a same-module control was Accepted. Nothing in the v2 front end constructed the fold_list qualified-name spine that v2.std.qualified_name qualified_name_from_node reads and v2.compiler.resolve try_resolve_qualified_name_node resolves -- that arm had a consumer and no producer, which is also why its own fabricated fallback (see refusal_reason_minted_as_canonical_identity) was never observed.",
    "REPAIR, landed in the same change: v2.compiler.body_lowering_fold body_lower_dotted_reference_optional lowers every chain of bare segments (head plus one or more dot-suffixes, every suffix slot EMPTY) to the fold_list qualified-name spine built by v2.std.algebra fold_list_node, in the body operand reader, the postfix dispatch and the fn-body chain; body_lower_qualified_name_production_spine_optional does the same for a multi-segment dag_surface_qualified_name in type position; and dag_token_dot is no longer admitted as a binary operator. Lowering does not decide what the chain denotes: field access over a parameter and a module path are one containment relation (docs/plans/namespace-resolution-design.md section 3) and the resolver's unique-on-chain rule (section 13) is the one place with the scope to decide.",
    "RUNG FOUND AT: outside the ladder -- silent wrongness. The lowering Accepted a program whose body it had rewritten to a different reference.",
    "CEILING: structurally guaranteed. Whether a lowered node spells every segment of the surface chain it came from is decidable on the pair. The interim wall is mechanically preventable: v2.test.claim.namespace_xl0.call_argument_mention_survival asserts the WHOLE spelling reaches the collector and that no segment appears as a mention of its own; v2.test.claim.namespace_xl0.cross_module_reference_resolution asserts the full chain survives to the resolver: a declared cross-module target is FOUND and refused identity-unrepresentable (distinct from an undeclared one, which refuses unbound), and a same-module control stays Accepted.",
    "NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, naming the capability: the forward body producer derived from the grammar's own rows (v2.compiler.body_producer_forward, general-body-producer-design section 3) replacing the hand-walker, so that a postfix chain's lowering is the grammar relation row for dag_grammar_postfix_dot_suffix_expr read forward and a truncating arm has no place to be written. A chain whose LAST segment carries a call or brace suffix stays with call_expression_erased_at_v2_body_lowering's trigger; this row's repair deliberately answers Absent for it.",
  ],
  evidence: [
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.compiler.body_lowering_fold", decl_name: "body_lower_dotted_reference_optional", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.compiler.body_lowering_fold", decl_name: "body_lower_qualified_name_production_spine_optional", field: WholeDeclaration },
  ],
}
